      "writtenOn": "2022-03-04T18:30:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will end up setting `*id` to the shifted value. The full id is the value before shifting `((spi_buf[1] \u003c\u003c 8) | spi_buf[2])`, so that\u0027s the one we want to return. The reason the shifting was added is because the [lower four bits are a manufacturing ID](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2bbc8a31546c76072c2f2f388b2db7c1a8d78200/driver/fingerprint/fpc/bep/fpc1025_private.h#9) that are OK to vary. However, if we\u0027re trying to get the ID we should get the full ID. If you change it back to how it was before it should be good:\n\n```\nsensor_id \u003d ((spi_buf[1] \u003c\u003c 8) | spi_buf[2]);\nif ((sensor_id \u003e\u003e 4) !\u003d FP_SENSOR_HWID) {\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 134,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "2bbc8a31546c76072c2f2f388b2db7c1a8d78200",
